  "description": "I’ve heard of epilepsy, but epilepsy?\n\nAs a second-year middle school student in a rural town, during a time when I was at my most sensitive, epilepsy, an unwelcome guest, suddenly arrived. Plagued by a barrage of medication side effects, and branded with the label “the kid who has seizures,” I had to live my days surrounded by misunderstanding and prejudice. \n\nA chaotic, headlong account of my battle with epilepsy, as I navigate daily life while facing this unfamiliar disease! (With a bit of information thrown in, though).\n\n(Source: KakaoPage, translated)",
